  "description": "XEXQIC crystallizes in the triclinic crystal system with space group P -1. Reported CIF formula moiety: C91 H86 Gd3 N5 Ni5 O27,5(C1 H4 O1),4(H2 O1). From the CIF bond table, Gd1 (Gd) has 8 O neighbors; Gd2 (Gd) has 8 O neighbors; Gd3 (Gd) has 8 O neighbors; Ni1 (Ni) has 5 O neighbors; Ni2 (Ni) has 5 O neighbors; Ni3 (Ni) has 5 O neighbors; Ni4 (Ni) has 5 O neighbors; Ni5 (Ni) has 5 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 15 pairs, 1 components; largest component is a network with cycles with three-dimensional metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.111-3.910 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 86.70-110.33°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula [Gd3Ni5L5(PhCOO)3(μ3-OH)5(μ3-OCH3)(CH3OH)4(H2O)]·5CH3OH·4H2O. Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 5 μ3-OH (explicit grouped unit in article formula), 1 H2O (explicit grouped unit in article formula).",
